<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dandanaqan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1040">1040</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dandanaqan was fought in 1040 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a> and the Ghaznavid army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mas'ud. The Seljuks won a decisive victory. It gave them control of Khurasan and marked the foundation of the Seljuk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dandanaqan.jpg" alt="Battle of Dandanaqan" width="300" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaznaly-seljuk_Dandanaqan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The army's weakness appeared under his son Mas'ud I, whose heavy columns, slowed by baggage and elephants, could not pin down the mobile Seljuk Turkmen horsemen, who finally defeated them at the <b>Battle of Dandanaqan</b> in 1040.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 1040, as the Seljuks defeated the Ghaznavids at the <b>Battle of Dandanaqan</b>, Ibrahim ibn Nasr, known as Böritegin and later as Tamghach Khan, took control of Bukhara and Samarqand.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The decisive moment came at the <b>Battle of Dandanaqan</b> in 1040, where Tughril and Chaghri routed the army of the Ghaznavid sultan Masud I, securing Khorasan and opening the Iranian plateau to Seljuk expansion.</blockquote><a href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
